From e7813e23b8fabdc7379c8682cfaa2b4475f210ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirill Mitrofanov <kmitrqq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:29:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: keep the stream rate for WSA V/I
 feedback

All backends are forced to 48 kHz, but the speaker protection VI module
tuning (static config, thermal and excursion filters) is for 8 kHz V/I
feedback, which is how the vendor graphs run it. Let WSA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0
use the frontend rate so the topology can pick 8 kHz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index c661c55..02a69b8 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -84,6 +84,14 @@ static int x1e80100_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	struct snd_interval *channels = hw_param_interval(params,
 							  SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS);
 
+	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case WSA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
+		/* Speaker V/I feedback runs at the rate the protection expects (8 kHz) */
+		return 0;
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
-- 
2.56.0

